---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
const base = '';
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms and Conditions" description="ThesisArcPro Terms and Conditions — rules and guidelines for using our service.">
  <Header />

  <main>
    <section class="policy-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <h1>Terms and Conditions</h1>
        <p>Last updated: July 2026</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-content">
      <div class="container policy-inner">

        <div class="policy-section">
          <h2>Welcome to ThesisArcPro</h2>
          <p>We provide you ("you", "your", "yours", or "Customer") access to our learning and educational consulting services ("Service") through our website, mobile website, and related web applications (collectively, the "Website"). These Terms and Conditions ("Terms") form a legally binding agreement between you and ThesisArcPro.</p>
          <p>ThesisArcPro is an educational consulting platform that connects Customers with academic Experts to assist in learning, research, and skill improvement. Before accessing or using our Services, please read these Terms carefully. By accessing or using the Website, you confirm that you have read, understood, and agreed to be bound by these Terms and our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="/payment-policy">Payment Policy</a>. If you do not agree, you must immediately cease using the Website.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-section">
          <h2>1. Interpretation & Definitions</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>"Website"</strong> refers to ThesisArcPro, including its web applications, mobile platforms, and customer portals.</li>
            <li><strong>"Customer," "User," or "You"</strong> refers to any individual accessing the Site, submitting an Order, or utilizing any free or paid Services.</li>
            <li><strong>"Expert"</strong> refers to an independent academic consultant or freelance specialist engaged to fulfill Custom Writing and consulting Services for Customers.</li>
            <li><strong>"Content"</strong> means all text, graphics, images, data, links, software, or other materials accessible through the Website.</li>
            <li><strong>"Order"</strong> refers to the electronic request for a paid Service submitted by the Customer specifying scope, deadline, sources, and assignment parameters.</li>
            <li><strong>"Personal Balance"</strong> refers to the total amount of withdrawable funds deposited into your account via supported payment methods.</li>
            <li><strong>"Escrow"</strong> refers to the financial arrangement where ThesisArcPro holds Order funds as a neutral third party, releasing them to the Expert only upon satisfactory completion of service milestones.</li>
            <li><strong>"Product"</strong> refers to the final deliverable (e.g., custom paper draft, research guide, presentation, or analysis) provided to the Customer. Products are provided strictly as educational samples and model papers.</li>
            <li><strong>"Product Revision"</strong> refers to a request submitted by the Customer to modify the delivered Product based on initial Order specifications.</li>
            <li><strong>"Quality Assurance Department"</strong> refers to the internal department responsible for reviewing work quality, verifying compliance with guidelines, and mediating disputed claims.</li>
            <li><strong>"AI Tools & Detection Services"</strong> refers to automated utilities (AI writing, AI rewriting, AI detection, and plagiarism checking) hosted on or integrated into the Site.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-section">
          <h2>2. General Eligibility & Use Rules</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Age Requirements:</strong> By using this Site, you affirm that you are at least 16 years of age (or the age of legal majority in your jurisdiction). If you are under the legal majority age, you confirm that your parent or legal guardian has reviewed and accepted these Terms on your behalf.</li>
            <li><strong>Lawful Use Only:</strong> You agree to use the Website and Services exclusively for lawful, personal, and educational purposes. You agree not to use the platform in any manner that violates local, state, national, or international laws.</li>
            <li><strong>Academic Integrity:</strong> Services are intended solely to support learning, facilitate research, and improve academic writing skills. Products are model materials and must not be submitted directly as a student's own work to any educational institution.</li>
            <li><strong>Direct Interaction Rules:</strong> You agree to maintain respectful, professional communication with Experts and Support personnel. Harassment, abusive language, or soliciting Experts outside the ThesisArcPro platform is strictly prohibited.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-section">
          <h2>3. Account Registration & Verification</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Account Creation:</strong> To place an Order or track progress, you must register using a valid email address or linked login provider (e.g., Google or Apple ID).</li>
            <li><strong>Accurate Information:</strong> You agree to provide complete, accurate, and up-to-date account details. You may not register an account on behalf of anyone else.</li>
            <li><strong>Single Account Policy:</strong> Users are limited to one active account. Duplicate accounts discovered by system audits may be merged or suspended.</li>
            <li><strong>Account Security:</strong> You are solely responsible for keeping your login credentials confidential. Notify ThesisArcPro immediately if you suspect unauthorized access to your account.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-section">
          <h2>4. AI Tools and Automated Services</h2>
          <p>ThesisArcPro offers automated tools to assist users with content generation, rewriting, AI detection, and originality analysis.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Free Plan Limitations:</strong> Automated tools may include usage limits (such as character limits for prompts or maximum word limits for document scanning). ThesisArcPro reserves the right to modify these limits at any time.</li>
            <li><strong>AI Generation & Rewriting:</strong> Automated outputs are generated algorithmically based on user prompts. They are not manually reviewed or proofread by human editors. Outputs may contain factual inaccuracies, bias, or stylistic inconsistencies. Users are responsible for verifying generated text before relying on it.</li>
            <li><strong>AI Detection & Plagiarism Scanning:</strong> Automated analysis tools rely on external algorithmic databases and probabilistic models. While highly advanced, detection outputs are advisory and do not guarantee 100% accuracy. False positives or false negatives may occur.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-section">
          <h2>5. Order Placement & Fulfillment Process</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Completing the Order Form:</strong> Customers are responsible for providing clear, complete, and accurate instructions when placing an Order.</li>
            <li><strong>Word Count Standards:</strong> Unless specified otherwise, 1 page equals 275 words (double-spaced) or 550 words (single-spaced). PowerPoint presentation slides average 135 words per slide.</li>
            <li><strong>Providing Source Materials:</strong> If your Order requires specific research materials, textbooks, or custom datasets, you must upload them promptly upon placing the Order. Failure to provide essential materials in a timely manner may result in delivery delays or require deadline extensions.</li>
            <li><strong>Instruction Changes:</strong> Instructions cannot be modified once an Expert has commenced work. Any additional scope requirements added after project kickoff may require additional fees.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-section">
          <h2>6. Payment Terms & Financial Policies</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Pricing & Service Fees:</strong> Prices are calculated dynamically based on project scope, academic level, complexity, and deadline urgency. The final total—including any non-refundable platform service fees—will be displayed at checkout.</li>
            <li><strong>Currency:</strong> Transactions and account balances are denominated in USD. You are responsible for any foreign exchange or conversion fees charged by your issuing bank.</li>
            <li><strong>Payment Gateways:</strong> Orders are processed via secure third-party payment gateways (including major credit card providers). ThesisArcPro does not store complete credit card or financial credentials on its servers.</li>
            <li><strong>Escrow Holding:</strong> Payments made for an Order are held in Escrow and released to the Expert upon project approval or automatically 8 days after the final deadline if no revision or dispute has been raised.</li>
            <li><strong>Promotional Balances:</strong> Bonus funds, promo credits, or rewards issued by ThesisArcPro hold no cash value, are non-transferable, and can only be used toward future Orders on ThesisArcPro.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-section">
          <h2>7. Order Delivery & Revision Policy</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Delivery Method:</strong> Completed Products are delivered digitally via your ThesisArcPro account dashboard under the Completed Orders tab, accompanied by email notifications.</li>
            <li><strong>Review Window:</strong> Customers are encouraged to thoroughly review delivered Products upon receipt.</li>
            <li><strong>Free Revisions:</strong> For standard projects under 10 pages, free revisions may be requested within 14 calendar days of delivery. For larger projects (over 10 pages/slides), free revisions may be requested within 30 calendar days of delivery.</li>
            <li>Revision instructions must align with original Order instructions. Requests introducing completely new scope or guidelines will be treated as additional editing orders and billed accordingly.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-section">
          <h2>8. Account Suspension, Deactivation & Deletion</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Deactivation by Customer:</strong> You may deactivate your account at any time via Account Settings → Deactivate Account. A 14-day hold period applies before permanent deletion.</li>
            <li><strong>Termination by Company:</strong> ThesisArcPro reserves the right to suspend or terminate accounts that breach these Terms, engage in payment disputes/chargebacks, upload malicious files, or attempt to bypass platform escrow channels.</li>
            <li><strong>Data Retention:</strong> Following account deletion, certain transaction and logging data may be retained in accordance with applicable laws for legal, tax, and audit compliance.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-section">
          <h2>9. Intellectual Property & Acceptable Product Use</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Model Content Ownership:</strong> All Products delivered by ThesisArcPro are custom reference materials provided strictly as examples for learning, research, and skill development.</li>
            <li><strong>Ownership Post-Delivery:</strong> Intellectual property rights in original deliverables transfer to the Customer upon full payment release, subject to fair usage guidelines and non-commercial educational reference.</li>
            <li><strong>Refunded Deliverables:</strong> If an order is canceled or fully refunded, the Customer loses all rights to use, cite, or edit the provided Product drafts. Unused refunded materials remain the property of ThesisArcPro.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-section">
          <h2>10. Limitation of Liability & Indemnification</h2>
          <p><strong>Disclaimer:</strong> The Services and Content on ThesisArcPro are provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis without warranties of any kind, either express or implied.</p>
          <p><strong>Liability Cap:</strong> To the maximum extent permitted by law, ThesisArcPro and its affiliates shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, or consequential damages, including loss of data, academic penalties, or business interruption arising from your use of the Services.</p>
          <p><strong>Indemnification:</strong> You agree to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless ThesisArcPro, its officers, directors, employees, and Experts from any claims, losses, or legal expenses resulting from your violation of these Terms or misuse of delivered Products.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-section">
          <h2>11. Amendments to Terms</h2>
          <p>ThesisArcPro reserves the right to modify or update these Terms and Conditions at any time. Major revisions will be announced via website notice or email prior to taking effect. Your continued use of the Website following notice of updates constitutes acceptance of the modified Terms.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-section">
          <h2>Contact Us</h2>
          <p>For any questions regarding these Terms and Conditions:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Email: <a href="mailto:thesisarcpro069@gmail.com">thesisarcpro069@gmail.com</a></li>
            <li>WhatsApp: <a href="https://wa.me/16624002088">+1 (662) 400-2088</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.policy-hero { background: var(--navy); padding: 10rem 0 4rem; text-align: center; }
.policy-hero h1 { color: var(--white); margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
.policy-hero p { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size: 0.9rem; }
.policy-content { padding: var(--section-padding); background: var(--off-white); }
.policy-inner { max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; }
.policy-section { background: rgb(229, 234, 238); border-radius: 12px; padding: 2rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
.policy-section h2 { color: var(--navy); font-size: 1.2rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; padding-bottom: 0.5rem; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--gold); }
.policy-section p { color: var(--text-mid); line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
.policy-section ul { color: var(--text-mid); line-height: 1.8; padding-left: 1.5rem; }
.policy-section ul li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
.policy-section a { color: var(--gold); text-decoration: none; }
.policy-section a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
</style>